# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything that RUNS ON THE PI must be checked out with LF, always.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without these
# rules every script here gets CRLF on checkout. They are then scp'd to the Pi,
# where the shebang reads `#!/bin/bash\r` and Linux reports:
#
#     bash: ./setup_kiosk.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# The `^M` is easy to miss and the error does not say "line endings". Python is
# just as exposed: `./bench_move.py` and `./burst_probe.py` are executed
# directly, so their shebangs matter too, even though the interpreter would
# otherwise tolerate CRLF.
#
# Added 2026-08-10, after `git add` warned it was about to do exactly this to
# the newly written kiosk scripts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.ino       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf

# Binary -- never touch these.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.pcap      binary
*.ply       binary
*.bin       binary
